  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let $P\\left(a t^{2}, 2 a t\\right), Q,$ R(ar $^{2}, 2ar)$ be three points on a parabola $y^{2}=4 a x$. If $P Q$ is the focal chord and $P K, Q R$ are parallel where the co-ordinates of $K$ is $(2 a, 0)$ then the value of $r$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "9DJqy",
      "text": "$\\frac{t}{1-t^{2}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4agri",
      "text": "$\\frac{1-t^{2}}{t}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1sbxD",
      "text": "$\\frac{t^{2}+1}{t}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZCcGZ",
      "text": "$\\frac{t^{2}-1}{t}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here, coordinate of $Q$ will be $\\left(\\frac{a}{t^{2}}, \\frac{-2 a}{t}\\right)$\r\nSlope of $Q R=\\frac{2}{r-\\frac{1}{t}}$\r\nSlope of $P K=\\frac{2 a t}{a t^{2}-2 a}=\\frac{2 t}{t^{2}-2}$\r\nsince, slope of $Q R=$ slope of $P K$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{2}{r-\\frac{1}{t}}=\\frac{2 t}{t^{2}-2}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad r=\\frac{t^{2}-1}{t}$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2018_mat_a47.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
